{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DFrameRungOnePhase","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameRungOnePhase","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.qbeta_counit_vs_trace"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.generatorWeight_unpinned_at_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.generatorWeight_unpinned_at_classical","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameRungOnePhase.lean#L113-L127","doc":"Sharpness of `h ≠ 0`: at the classical point `h = 0` the weight is\ngenuinely unpinned — (D1) holds for EVERY `w`.\n\nThis is the same degeneracy the corpus records when it warns that a theorem\nevaluated only at the classical point `q = 1` is convention-agnostic by\naccident of sitting on the coincidence, so it says nothing about which\nconvention is right.\n\nNote this needs NO `(2 : K) ≠ 0`: at `h = 0` both sides vanish even in\ncharacteristic two, so the lemma is strictly stronger than (D1) is there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.generatorWeight_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.generatorWeight_forced","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameRungOnePhase.lean#L94-L111","doc":"**The falsifiable content.** Leave the Ocneanu weight on the sigma-\ngenerators as an unknown `w`; then (D1) holds **iff** `w = z`.\n\nSo the rung-1 phase does not merely happen to equal the gap — it PINS the\nMarkov parameter. This is the precise form of the claim that `z` enters the\nfive-rung ladder in exactly one place, and it is what stops\n`rungOnePhase_eq_counit_sub_trace` from being arithmetic on chosen constants.\n\n`h ≠ 0` is necessary and its sharpness is recorded below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.rungOnePhase_eq_counit_sub_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.rungOnePhase_eq_counit_sub_trace","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameRungOnePhase.lean#L80-L92","doc":"**(D1).** Twice the rung-1 phase is exactly the counit-minus-trace gap on\nthe neutron−proton difference, identically in both variables.\n\nThis is the bridge the corpus was missing: `eps_sub_trMNP` gives the gap as\n`h*(z-1)`, and this identifies that gap with `2*alpha`. Together they make\n`alpha` derived rather than asserted.\n\n`(2 : K) ≠ 0` is necessary — see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.rungOnePhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.rungOnePhase","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameRungOnePhase.lean#L71-L78","doc":"The Q_beta ladder's rung-1 phase, `alpha = (z-1)*h/2`.\n\nStated over a general field with `z` and `h` free — unlike\n`EigenphaseCarrierVacuity.eigenphase`, which is pinned to the excised\nconvention C via `markovZC`, and unlike `BraidImageEigenphaseExclusion.alphaOf`,\nwhich is `ℝ`- and function-valued. A claim holding \"identically in q and z\"\nneeds the free form. ","signatureChunk":0}]}